# Strumming: 6/8 (repertoire plan: st-strum-6-8). An original strumming study.
# Your part: Em (022000), C (x32010), D (xx0232), Em, four bars each. Count six quick eighths in
# two groups of three: down on 1, down on 2, up on 3, down on 4, down on 5, up on 6, and strum
# beats 1 and 4 a little harder. SixTab cannot mark an accent on a slash, so the accents are in
# the words above the first bar, and the teacher's bass plays on 1 and 4 (root, then fifth) to
# make the two-beat sway audible. Tempo 84 quarters is a dotted quarter of 56.
